{"study_accession":"PRJNA1004569","secondary_study_accession":"SRP454631","title":"Human Leukocyte Antigen Genotyping and Expression Analysis with Nanopore Long-Read Sequencing","description":"Human leukocyte antigen (HLA) typing plays a critical role in evaluating donor-recipient compatibility prior to hematopoietic cell transplantation (HCT) to minimize the risk of rejection and graft versus host disease (GVHD). Compared to traditional sequence-based methods for HLA typing, next-generation sequencing offers significant advantages in terms of accuracy, turnaround time, and cost. Here, we sought to evaluate the performance of nanopore long-read sequencing for HLA typing and HLA expression analysis, including the identification of HLA transcript isoforms. To that end, we used nanopore long-read sequencing to perform RNA-seq on primary lymphocytes isolated from peripheral blood from 12 human donors.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":15,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN36946613","study_accession":"PRJNA1004569","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"not collected","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-08-18","attributes":[["isolate","donor001"],["age","not collected"],["biomaterial_provider","Eric Weimer, University of North Carolina Hospitals, 101 Manning Drive, Room 1053, East Wing, Chapel Hill, NC, 27514"],["collection_date","not collected"],["geo_loc_name","USA: North Carolina"],["sex","not collected"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","lymphocyte"],["health_state","healthy"],["replicate","1"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25610315","experiment_accession":"SRX21337416","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"MinION","read_count":2627191,"base_count":2175985784,"first_public":"2023-08-18","experiment_title":"MinION sequencing: RNA-seq of Homo sapiens peripheral blood lymphoc